  Description: 'The open water south of Rice Point, St Peters and the East Water:
    a shelf twenty metres down under the north edge, then the bottom falls away to
    the deep mud where the draggers work. Nothing out here to hit, and nothing to
    hide behind when it blows. NAME OWED: the owner names the water scenes in PEI-variant
    style (world-map-plan 7 Q4); the id is stable whatever he picks.'
